WEBVTT

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:06.150
Thanks for having me!

00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:09.980
<i>Doesn't this guy ever get nervous?</i>

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:13.050
Okay, then! Are all the first-years here?

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:14.490
Hey, Iwashimizu.

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:16.100
H-Hello...

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:22.940
I'm Sekizan Takuya, the team's captain.

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:23.750
Nice to meet you.

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:26.460
That guy's the captain?

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.520
<i>H-He looks really scary.</i>

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:31.130
I'm the vice-captain, Hachioji Mutsumi.

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:36.410
We have a faculty adviser,
but most of the time, it's just us.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:39.430
Now, let's introduce ourselves...

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.830
Well...

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:46.440
Since there are a lot of us,
you can learn our names as we go along.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:48.940
<b>Boo</b>

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:48.940
<b>We have our reasons, like pacing...</b>

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:48.940
<b>Boo</b>

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:48.940
You can't be serious!

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:51.360
First-years, tell us your names.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:52.860
And your position if you've played before.

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:55.860
We'll start with you.

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:58.030
I'm Gion! Sir!

00:00:58.430 --> 00:01:02.050
Yup, Gion Kenji-kun. No previous experience.

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:03.150
Next.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:05.920
You're big.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:11.420
I-I'm Iwashimizu Sumiaki. Um...

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:12.700
How tall are you?

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:14.210
One... One...

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:16.130
1.9 meters.

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:17.760
Your position?

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:20.430
L-Lo...

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:21.450
Lock.

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:22.520
Okay, next.

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:24.790
I'm Hirano. This is my first time playing.

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:25.850
Okay, next.

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:28.260
I'm Kitamachi. I'm a beginner.

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:28.940
Next.

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:32.990
I'm Oharano. I played in grade and
middle school, and at rugby school.

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:34.690
I play fly-half.

00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:37.490
Two guys with experience? That's amazing.

00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:39.700
This year's crop looks pretty good.

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:43.480
Should we split up the first-years?

00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:44.670
Yeah.

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:48.560
I'm Hoakari Umeno, a second-year.

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:50.210
I'm the team manager.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:54.580
Okay. Beginners, go with Hachioji-senpai.

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:55.980
Follow me.

00:01:57.340 --> 00:01:59.260
Experienced players with me.

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:00.310
Yes, sir.

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:03.230
Everybody else will be doing core training.

00:02:03.230 --> 00:02:04.620
Get going.

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:14.110
<i>I hope Gion-kun behaves himself...</i>

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:19.110
We'll start by getting you guys
 used to handling the ball.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:22.900
It's lighter than I thought.

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:24.980
It makes a sound like a basketball.

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:27.230
You probably haven't felt one before.

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:29.000
They're not brown, I've noticed.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:31.530
You mean the leather ones?

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:33.660
You're thinking of the old-style balls.

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:35.470
Try throwing it around.

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:40.250
It bounces so strangely!

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:42.340
Doesn't it? Hilarious!

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:45.970
Hey! I want to tackle someone!

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:46.820
Huh?

00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:47.730
What?

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:50.050
We're not practicing tackling yet.

00:02:50.050 --> 00:02:51.110
Why not?

00:02:50.050 --> 00:02:51.600
<i>He's already at it...</i>

00:02:51.110 --> 00:02:52.260
Just because.

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:53.960
You taught me how yesterday.

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:56.970
I'm not sure that really
counted as teaching...

00:02:58.090 --> 00:03:02.360
You're even more difficult than
my brother in fourth grade.

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:03.980
Just let me do it—

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:06.870
Respect your elders.

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:10.280
You should learn from your mistakes.

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:12.880
You're starting to get me down.

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:18.700
We want energetic players.

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:22.770
But we don't want any
that lack basic manners.

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:32.950
I want to do it...

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:37.980
I want to tackle someone.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:41.170
Just talking to myself!

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:42.740
I was just talking to myself, sir!

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:45.740
Fine.

00:03:50.130 --> 00:03:54.250
If you're that desperate to 
tackle someone, tackle me.

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:55.580
Sekizan?

00:03:56.910 --> 00:03:58.590
Really? Sir?

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:02.380
Wh-What is that beginner blabbering about?

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:03.720
Is he looking down on us?

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:08.970
<i>I doubt he'd do anything to 
hurt a first-year, but...</i>

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:31.230
You can give me everything you've got!

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:27.590
<b>Episode 2 
I Want to Tackle Someone</b>

00:06:30.190 --> 00:06:31.700
Ouch!

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:33.340
Gion-kun!

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:43.790
Damn you!

00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:45.050
That's enough—

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:53.430
You're going nowhere.

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:55.100
Listen closely, Kyoto.

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:55.930
His name's Gion.

00:06:57.770 --> 00:07:00.550
If you can complete the training drill
I'm about to give you,

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:03.560
I'll reward you with
five chances a day to tackle me.

00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:05.570
"Training drill"?

00:07:07.770 --> 00:07:08.530
The turtle.

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:12.140
Oh, I see.

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:15.690
Mutsumi, show him.

00:07:15.690 --> 00:07:16.870
Roger.

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:19.960
Let's start practice.

00:07:27.620 --> 00:07:29.100
What the hell is this?

00:07:29.100 --> 00:07:31.400
Now, now. Don't move.

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:36.980
While maintaining that pose,
go to the other end of the field and back.

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:37.970
What?

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:40.020
Keep doing reps until I tell you to stop.

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:42.140
Is there any point to doing this?

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:43.520
I want to practice tackling—

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:46.980
Sekizan never makes his players 
do anything for no reason.

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:52.630
Are you going to do it or not?

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:54.870
I'll do it.

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:56.460
I'll be back... sir.

00:07:56.460 --> 00:07:58.620
Okie-doke. See you later.

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:04.740
Don't let your knees touch the ground.

00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:07.210
Y-Yes, sir. This is hard.

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:11.650
You guys, try throwing the ball 
around like you're playing catch.

00:08:11.650 --> 00:08:12.930
Y-Yes, sir!

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:15.960
Sekizan, how long should 
we keep him doing it?

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:18.760
Until practice is over.

00:08:20.690 --> 00:08:22.020
Gotcha.

00:08:29.560 --> 00:08:31.180
What <i>is</i> he doing?

00:08:31.180 --> 00:08:32.950
He doesn't even have any muscles.

00:08:32.950 --> 00:08:35.970
Oh, jeez, Gion-kun...

00:08:36.690 --> 00:08:39.000
Are you guys from the same middle school?

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:42.320
Oh, no. Um...

00:08:42.320 --> 00:08:43.460
It's Oharano.

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:44.900
S-Sorry.

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:48.670
He's pretty much a disgrace, isn't he?

00:08:49.820 --> 00:08:51.940
You two, come over here.

00:08:51.940 --> 00:08:53.310
Ah, yes, sir.

00:08:58.220 --> 00:09:00.650
This is hard, dammit.

00:09:11.130 --> 00:09:12.460
Good, good.

00:09:12.460 --> 00:09:14.040
You might have some talent for this.

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:17.240
Really? You're making me blush.

00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:20.120
Damn ball!

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:25.300
Okay, that's enough.

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:29.690
Awesome corkscrew.

00:09:29.690 --> 00:09:31.310
That's practically a tornado.

00:09:31.310 --> 00:09:34.260
Hey, Mutsumi. Finish up over there.

00:09:35.430 --> 00:09:37.380
That was way more fun than I expected.

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:39.760
Yeah, although I couldn't catch the ball.

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:40.780
Me neither.

00:09:41.610 --> 00:09:42.140
Sekizan.

00:09:43.230 --> 00:09:44.180
What about him?

00:10:00.520 --> 00:10:01.700
He's been doing that the whole time.

00:10:02.540 --> 00:10:04.120
For three hours straight?

00:10:12.010 --> 00:10:12.630
Hey.

00:10:13.980 --> 00:10:16.880
You've still got four tackles left for today.

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:18.720
I'll take 'em!

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:28.990
I'll take 'em tomorrow...

00:10:28.990 --> 00:10:30.950
Okay, good work today.

00:10:30.950 --> 00:10:33.670
Iwashimizu, help me carry him.

00:10:33.670 --> 00:10:34.900
Yes, sir.

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:49.620
Let's start by throwing
the ball around again today.

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:51.500
Don't worry about him.

00:10:52.170 --> 00:10:53.920
He's still doing it...

00:10:55.310 --> 00:10:58.670
<i>All right. That's twenty reps.</i>

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:08.640
I'll send you flying!

00:11:09.390 --> 00:11:11.900
Dammit!

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:51.500
Good work today.

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:52.690
Laters.

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:57.320
<b>Rugby Team</b>

00:12:13.780 --> 00:12:15.820
G-Gion-kun...

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:17.720
Huh?

00:12:17.720 --> 00:12:19.000
Are you okay?

00:12:19.780 --> 00:12:20.850
Yeah.

00:12:27.130 --> 00:12:30.530
You should start with something easier.

00:12:30.530 --> 00:12:33.700
Doing this crazy training regimen
will make you hate rugby—

00:12:33.700 --> 00:12:35.020
What are you babbling about?

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:38.650
I'm practicing to play rugby.

00:12:38.650 --> 00:12:40.150
What?

00:12:41.290 --> 00:12:43.610
I understand everything now.

00:12:44.130 --> 00:12:46.840
I know how to tackle!

00:12:48.010 --> 00:12:50.990
<b>Yes</b>

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:50.990
<b>I shall call this: 
Gion Road</b>

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:50.990
<b>Just focus 
on practice</b>

00:12:51.640 --> 00:12:54.000
<b>Tree Trunk, 
carry me!!</b>

00:12:52.430 --> 00:12:54.000
<b>N-</b>

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:54.000
<b>No thanks...</b>

00:12:57.010 --> 00:12:59.110
How to tackle?

00:13:00.350 --> 00:13:04.220
I was watching them practice tackling
while doing the turtle.

00:13:05.190 --> 00:13:06.980
Your head's too low.

00:13:06.980 --> 00:13:08.350
You won't knock anyone down like that.

00:13:14.060 --> 00:13:15.710
That's it.

00:13:15.710 --> 00:13:18.270
Good tackles made a different sound.

00:13:18.270 --> 00:13:19.020
Next.

00:13:19.810 --> 00:13:24.280
When their tackles <i>sounded</i> good,
 their backs were straight.

00:13:24.910 --> 00:13:27.410
They weren't just
crashing into their opponent.

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:29.030
They went in like arrows.

00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:32.150
Building good posture!

00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:34.750
That was the point of doing the turtle.

00:13:35.810 --> 00:13:38.430
<i>Gion-kun's learning...</i>

00:13:38.430 --> 00:13:42.050
But even if I could pull off
a tackle like that,

00:13:43.470 --> 00:13:45.830
I don't think it'll be enough
to take him down.

00:13:48.050 --> 00:13:50.090
He's way bigger than me.

00:13:52.380 --> 00:13:55.410
Well, that problem...

00:13:56.330 --> 00:13:59.270
<b>Stare</b>

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:00.860
I've got it!

00:14:01.300 --> 00:14:02.980
Let me practice on you!

00:14:03.440 --> 00:14:04.180
What?

00:14:05.330 --> 00:14:08.820
You're at least as tall as that mophead.

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:11.040
Y-Yeah, but...

00:14:11.040 --> 00:14:16.040
And I can't practice tackling on my own.

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:19.490
I'm glad you're the perfect size.

00:14:23.080 --> 00:14:25.710
I'll definitely knock him off his feet!

00:14:27.240 --> 00:14:28.050
Yeah.

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:31.730
Let's do it.

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:35.970
I'm beat.

00:14:38.150 --> 00:14:40.770
Hachi-san, look.

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:44.670
He's starting to look pretty good.

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:47.900
That's enough for today.

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:49.330
All right!

00:14:51.340 --> 00:14:53.280
I'm ready for my tackles, sir!

00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:55.870
I thought you would've 
learned your lesson by now.

00:14:57.690 --> 00:14:58.540
Yes, sir!

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:03.670
Bring it on, then.

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:15.760
<i>He's small, but he's strong.</i>

00:15:19.710 --> 00:15:20.810
<i>He has good instincts, too.</i>

00:15:22.990 --> 00:15:28.900
<i>Over the past few days, 
he's been getting better.</i>

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:33.950
<i>And more than anything, he's competitive.</i>

00:15:36.870 --> 00:15:37.650
<i>But...</i>

00:15:41.790 --> 00:15:44.420
You'll never knock me down like that.

00:15:53.860 --> 00:15:57.160
Finished already, first-year?

00:15:57.160 --> 00:15:58.930
Gion-kun...

00:16:03.420 --> 00:16:05.940
This is your last tackle.

00:16:13.900 --> 00:16:15.750
Just give up—

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:20.950
Th-That's it!

00:16:20.950 --> 00:16:23.150
Not even the captain can 
ride out a tackle like that.

00:16:27.300 --> 00:16:30.170
Ultimate technique complete!

00:16:30.930 --> 00:16:35.430
<i>No matter how big they are,
they're not that muscly below the knees.</i>

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:42.680
<i>I'll throw all my weight there
and fly in like an arrow down low!</i>

00:16:53.800 --> 00:16:55.200
Sekizan...

00:17:05.640 --> 00:17:09.460
That wasn't "below the knees." 
Those were his heels.

00:17:14.130 --> 00:17:15.220
How was that?

00:17:17.470 --> 00:17:21.720
Looking beat before the fifth tackle was
a ploy to make you let your guard down.

00:17:25.030 --> 00:17:26.200
Are you okay?

00:17:28.200 --> 00:17:29.150
Gion-kun?

00:17:29.150 --> 00:17:30.230
That tackle...

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:34.240
...felt awesome!

00:17:35.790 --> 00:17:37.530
Don't be so reckless.

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:43.790
Your back muscles are incredible.

00:17:44.570 --> 00:17:46.190
Were you working out beforehand?

00:17:46.600 --> 00:17:48.120
Now that you mention it...

00:17:48.820 --> 00:17:53.810
For years, I've been dangling from
horizontal bars to make myself taller.

00:17:54.670 --> 00:17:57.520
I had nothing else to do up there,
so I'd do pull-ups.

00:17:57.520 --> 00:17:58.130
Could that be it?

00:18:04.060 --> 00:18:06.020
Must be. I see now.

00:18:06.390 --> 00:18:08.420
Seriously?

00:18:08.420 --> 00:18:12.270
Don't laugh at me, dammit!

00:18:12.270 --> 00:18:13.670
Let's clean up.

00:18:13.670 --> 00:18:15.570
Yes, sir.

00:18:15.580 --> 00:18:17.260
I can't move.

00:18:19.690 --> 00:18:21.740
Here comes the magic kettle.

00:18:21.740 --> 00:18:24.120
That's freezing! What was that for?

00:18:25.430 --> 00:18:26.540
For some reason,

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:30.260
everyone gets re-energized when I pour
water from this kettle over them.

00:18:30.260 --> 00:18:31.540
Therefore, it must be magic.

00:18:31.980 --> 00:18:34.050
What kind of reasoning is that?

00:18:35.130 --> 00:18:37.000
You're one of us now.

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:39.250
I wish Ume-chan would pour water over me...

00:18:39.250 --> 00:18:40.670
Nice one, first-year.

00:18:40.670 --> 00:18:42.410
Let's go home, guys.

00:18:48.630 --> 00:18:51.560
Sekizan, what do you make of
the first-years this year?

00:18:56.230 --> 00:18:57.800
<b>1 New Message</b>

00:18:57.800 --> 00:19:00.780
<b>From: </b>Keijo's Marukome<b> 
Sub: </b>Long time no see<b></b>

00:18:57.800 --> 00:19:00.780
We're playing again this year.
Our field, this Saturday!! 
Taira's so excited, he won't 
shut up about it, LOL.

00:19:01.850 --> 00:19:02.750
Mutsumi.

00:19:05.630 --> 00:19:09.170
Oh, right. It's that time of year already.

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:11.250
This year...

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:17.960
Keijo High

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:17.960
Saturday, 14:00

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:17.960
Meet @ 12:00, Jinko Front Gate

00:19:13.490 --> 00:19:17.960
This weekend, we have a practice game
against Keijo High.

00:19:17.960 --> 00:19:19.100
A game?!

00:19:19.100 --> 00:19:20.720
We're facing them again, huh?

00:19:20.720 --> 00:19:23.180
You mean, the team that
 destroyed us last year?

00:19:23.180 --> 00:19:27.090
Why does one of Kanagawa Prefecture's 
semifinalists even bother playing us?

00:19:27.090 --> 00:19:30.230
Their vice-captain took a shine to Sekizan.

00:19:33.170 --> 00:19:35.020
Sorry I'm late...

00:19:35.410 --> 00:19:38.740
Ebumi, what have you been 
doing this past week?

00:19:39.510 --> 00:19:41.090
I had a cold.

00:19:41.090 --> 00:19:43.020
Go do twenty laps of the field later.

00:19:43.020 --> 00:19:44.280
I knew it.

00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:45.410
Forty laps.

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:48.920
Forty's rough.

00:19:48.920 --> 00:19:51.290
We'll discuss our practice 
schedules separately.

00:19:51.700 --> 00:19:53.320
Split into forwards and backs.

00:19:53.320 --> 00:19:54.880
Yes, sir.

00:19:55.720 --> 00:19:58.220
Hey, Tree Trunk. Split into what?

00:20:00.580 --> 00:20:01.430
Tree Trunk?

00:20:01.910 --> 00:20:04.500
I'll explain it to you.

00:20:04.500 --> 00:20:06.890
Beginners, over here.

00:20:07.140 --> 00:20:27.780
<b>Backs</b>

00:20:07.140 --> 00:20:27.780
<b>Forwards</b>

00:20:08.470 --> 00:20:11.980
Rugby matches are fifteen versus fifteen.

